This product includes no third-party source. Every model here is a
from-scratch implementation, written against a reference rather than
translated from it, and verified against a captured oracle. What the
references contributed is described below, because "written against" is a real
debt even where it is not a copyright one.

  CosyVoice (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice
      The reference for `xabe-cosy`: the speech language model's prompt
      assembly, `ras_sampling`, the flow's DiT and Euler solver, the HiFT
      vocoder and its NSF source. `tools/convert_cosyvoice.py` reads its
      checkpoints and `tools/oracle/capture_cosyvoice.py` runs it to produce
      the oracle these are tested against.

  taiwanese_tonal_tlpa_tacotron2 (BSD-3-Clause),
  https://github.com/yfliao/taiwanese_tonal_tlpa_tacotron2
      The reference for `xabe-taco`, and the source of the checkpoints it
      reads: a Taiwanese tonal-TLPA retraining of NVIDIA's Tacotron2 and
      WaveGlow, whose BSD-3-Clause notice it carries (Copyright 2018 NVIDIA
      Corporation). Its `text/symbols.py` defines the 71-symbol alphabet
      `xabe_taco::text` reproduces, including what that alphabet silently
      drops; its `hparams.py` fixes the geometry; and its vendored `waveglow`
      supplies the class definitions `tools/convert_tacotron2.py` needs to
      unpickle a pre-1.6 torch object graph at all. It is also run, by
      `tools/oracle/capture_tacotron2.py`, to produce the oracle `xabe-taco`
      is tested against.

  whisper.cpp (MIT), https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
      The reference for the VAD segmenter's hysteresis constants and for
      several ASR decoding details. Its divergences from upstream Silero and
      from HuggingFace are recorded in `docs/MODEL.md` rather than copied.

  llmxabe, the same author's LLM engine
      The source of the NVRTC compile-and-cache pattern, the sm_75
      reachability constraints on the tensor-core path, the shared-memory
      stride arithmetic, and the serving crate's dependency set. See
      `docs/KERNELS.md`, `docs/TOOLCHAIN.md` and `docs/OPTIMIZATION.md`.

  Transformers, VITS, Silero VAD, Whisper, Llama
      References for the geometries in `docs/MODEL.md`, and in several cases
      the oracle a stage is compared against.

